<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
Lucide's `dumbbell` at the ratio the App Shortcuts Icon Design Guidelines set, a 24dp glyph in a 44dp
live area, carried onto the adaptive icon canvas. `AdaptiveIconDrawable` puts the masked viewport at
the inner 72dp of the 108dp layer, so the glyph is 72 x 24 / 44, or 39dp, centered. Note the adaptive
icon design page says 66dp in the same sentence, but that is the zone no mask shape may clip rather
than the viewport, and the 48dp floor it gives is for an app's brand logo, not a shortcut's glyph.
-->
